{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":127795,"duration_api_ms":127758,"num_turns":16,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"19c952fe-94d8-4c9f-af7b-2df75757aa0c","total_cost_usd":0.5173844999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":36758,"cache_read_input_tokens":287154,"output_tokens":5761,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":36758,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":9,"outputTokens":5761,"cacheReadInputTokens":287154,"cacheCreationInputTokens":36758,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.5173844999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed 6 amendments against the shrimp molt cycle, substrate model, and preset pipeline code. 5 of 6 are verified real defects: the molt_cycle mixed-outcome logic creates inconsistency between the boolean and accumulator (fr-2-da64408d), the legacy migration fires on fresh states causing immediate juvenile molts (fr-2-61c597e4), the boolean-based accumulator undercounts multi-stage failures (fr-2-1595155b), the detritus consumption magic constant is a configurability gap (fr-2-c7322f22), and the 5 new TOML knobs are dead configuration silently dropped by deserialization (fr-2-0b9a822f). One amendment (fr-2-ba1e4ade) proposing layer-by-layer porosity iteration is a modeling fidelity enhancement rather than a correctness fix.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-2-da64408d","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified at lines 498-510 of shrimp.rs. When any_failed && any_succeeded are both true on a mixed-outcome day: last_molt_success is set to false (line 501), failed_molt_accum goes +0.3 then -0.35 (net -0.05). The boolean says 'failure' while the accumulator shows improvement. Since last_molt_success gates sub-adult maturation (line 852), a juvenile molt failure on the same tick as an adult success blocks sub-adult maturation despite improving accumulator health. This is a real inconsistency with downstream behavioral impact."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-ba1e4ade","decision":"reject","rationale":"The function effective_substrate_porosity (lines 133-140) deliberately uses the surface layer's porosity as a first-order approximation for the Bouldin model. While the amendment correctly identifies that this loses accuracy for thin sand caps over aquasoil, this is a modeling simplification, not a bug. The suggested layer-by-layer iterative Bouldin approach is a significant algorithmic enhancement to improve model fidelity. The current behavior is physically defensible as a surface-dominated diffusion approximation and doesn't produce incorrect results per se - just less precise ones. This is an enhancement request, not a defect fix."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-c7322f22","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified at line 188-191 of substrate.rs. The detritus daily consumption fraction 0.01 is hardcoded while the analogous periphyton consumption fraction reads from process_params.microfauna_periphyton_consumption (line 151-153). This creates an asymmetry where one consumption pathway is tunable and the other is not. Extracting to a named constant with documentation is a minimal, safe improvement that prevents the magic number from being overlooked during tuning."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-61c597e4","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified by reading the code. AnimalState::default() sets inter_molt_timer_days=14.0 (biology.rs:615), StageCohort::default() sets molt_timer_days=0.0 (biology.rs:112). The migration guard at shrimp.rs:411-419 triggers whenever inter_molt_timer_days > 0 AND all stage timers are 0 - which is exactly the fresh default state. This copies 14.0 into all stage timers. Juvenile interval is 14 days, so timer_factor = 14/14 = 1.0, causing immediate molt on tick 1. This is a clear initialization bug: the legacy migration path was only meant for old saves but fires on every new simulation."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-1595155b","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified at lines 440-442 and 498-509. The any_failed/any_succeeded booleans collapse multi-stage outcomes into single +0.3/-0.35 adjustments regardless of how many stages resolved. With intervals 14/21/28, overlap days (LCM at 42, 84, etc.) can have 2-3 stages resolving simultaneously. Two failed stages add only +0.3 instead of +0.6, and a mixed day (failure + success) nets -0.05 on the accumulator. This makes mortality pressure inversely correlated with the number of molting stages - weakest when most of the population is molting. This is a distinct issue from fr-2-da64408d (which focuses on the boolean/accumulator inconsistency), and both warrant fixing."},{"amendment_id":"fr-2-0b9a822f","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified across all three files. ShrimpPreset (presets.rs:430-478) lacks ca_min_mg_per_l, mg_min_mg_per_l, juvenile_molt_interval_days, sub_adult_molt_interval_days, and molt_success_threshold fields. The TOML has them (lines 23-27). Without #[serde(deny_unknown_fields)], serde silently drops them. shrimp_preset_to_params (lib.rs:746-799) never copies them. While the ShrimpRuntimeParams defaults (biology.rs:719-737) happen to match the TOML values (20.0, 5.0, 14.0, 21.0, 0.55), the config is dead: editing these TOML values would have zero effect. This is a maintenance trap that silently breaks the preset customization contract."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"865b0e9b-83db-4a81-9848-36bbb6312bc3"}
